app/api/v1/routes.py (L66 to 74)
  Note: The helper returns only the first phone_number_id found in the entire webhook payload, even though payloads may contain multiple entries/changes.
```
def whatsapp_phone_number_id_from_payload(payload: dict[str, Any]) -> str | None:
    for entry in payload.get('entry', []):
        for change in entry.get('changes', []):
            value = change.get('value', {})
            metadata = value.get('metadata', {})
            phone_number_id = metadata.get('phone_number_id')
            if phone_number_id:
                return str(phone_number_id)
    return None
